    "lawCode": "Amd §65-b, ABC L; amd §§851 & 855, Cor L; amd §3-0301, En Con L; amd §261, Exec L; amd §3.09, Pks & Rec L; amd §1198, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4058\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, the correction\nlaw, the environmental conservation law, the executive law, the parks,\nrecreation and historic preservation law and the vehicle and traffic\nlaw, in relation to compensatory service\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill would change \"community service\" to \"compensatory service\"\nin certain alternative sentencing programs.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the bill amends paragraphs (a), (b), and (c) of\nsubdivision 3 and subdivision 4 of section 65-b of the alcoholic\nbeverage control law to replace \"community service\" to \"compensatory\nservice\" as a penalty for violation of the article.\n\nSection 2 of the bill amends paragraphs (a), (b), and (c) of\nsubdivision 2 and subdivision 3 of section 65-b of the alcoholic\nbeverage control law to replace \"community service\" to \"compensatory\nservice\" as a penalty for violation of the article.\n\nSection 3 of the bill amends subdivision 5 of section 851 of the\ncorrection law to replace \"community service program\" with\n\"compensatory services program\" for eligible inmates to participate in\noff premises service related activities.\n\nSection 4 of the bill amends subdivision 2 of section 855 of the\ncorrection law to replace \"community services program\" with\n\"compensatory services program\".\n\nSection 5 of the bill amends paragraph hh of subdivision 1 of section\n3-0301 of the environmental conservation law to replace \"community\nservice\" with \"compensatory service\".\n\nSection 6 of the bill amends paragraph b of subdivision 1 of section\n261 of the executive law to replace \"community service\" with\n\"compensatory service\".\n\nSection 7 of the bill amends subdivision 2-f of section 3.09 of the\nparks, recreation, and historic preservation law to replace \"community\nservice\" with \"compensatory service\".\n\nSection 8 of the bill amends paragraph (e) of subdivision 3 of section\n1198 of the vehicle and traffic law to replace \"community service\"\nwith \"compensatory service\".\n\nSection 9 of the bill provides for an effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis bill would replace the term \"community service\" with\n\"compensatory service.\" Presently, Justices throughout our state often\nimpose community service sentences in lieu of paying fines or, in some\ncases, serving jail time. This term implies an aura of civic\nresponsibility, as most who perform community service do so\nvoluntarily and out of kindness. The criminal defendant, on the other\nhand, is mandated to contribute his or her time to community programs\nin lieu of paying a fine or going to jail. It is extremely doubtful\nthat many of those presently sentenced to \"community service\" would do\nsuch work on their own without a Court mandate. Their actions\ntherefore should be given a different terminology than those who\nvoluntarily perform community service.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007: A.3882/S.2372 - Passed Both Houses, Veto No. 56\n2005-2006:  A.1254/S.6991- Passed Both Houses, Veto No. 244\n2003-2004: A.5118 - Passed Assembly/S.2576 - Committed to Rules\n2001-2002: A.336-A - Passed Assembly/S.7601- Referred to Rules\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
